NAME
    gcloud alpha biglake hive catalogs - manage BigLake Hive catalogs

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha biglake hive catalogs COMMAND [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Manage BigLake Hive catalogs.

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --help.

    Run $ gcloud help for details.

COMMANDS
    COMMAND is one of the following:

     create
        (ALPHA) Create a BigLake Hive catalog.

     delete
        (ALPHA) Delete a BigLake Hive catalog.

     describe
        (ALPHA) Describe a BigLake Hive catalog.

     get-iam-policy
        (ALPHA) Get the IAM policy for a BigLake Hive catalog.

     list
        (ALPHA) List BigLake Hive catalogs.

     set-iam-policy
        (ALPHA) Set the IAM policy for a BigLake Hive catalog.

     update
        (ALPHA) Update a BigLake Hive catalog.

NOTES
    This command is currently in alpha and might change without notice. If this
    command fails with API permission errors despite specifying the correct
    project, you might be trying to access an API with an invitation-only early
    access allowlist.

